            "raw_output": "360:        random_vert_flip: If True, randomly flip images vertically during training.\n410:        random_vert_flip: bool = False,\n433:        self.random_vert_flip = random_vert_flip\n612:        applies channel masking and optional vertical flip, then assembles the sample\n650:        if self.random_vert_flip and torch.bernoulli(torch.ones(()) / 2) == 1:\n651:            sample[\"ts\"] = np.flip(sample[\"ts\"], axis=-2).copy()\n653:                sample[\"forecast\"] = np.flip(sample[\"forecast\"], axis=-2).copy()",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01KoXjcA2ydsDnGfJgMnUcuP",
            "title": "grep -n \"flip\\|vflip\\|vertical\" helio.py",
            "kind": "execute"
