      "time": 1789412963.8689296,
      "body": "Yes. Since the flip is now baked into `__getitem__`, `item['ts']` is already the flipped version \u2014 flipping it back (`np.flip` twice = identity) gives you the original.\n\nLook at cell 32 in `0_dataset_dataloader_template.ipynb` (the plotting cell). Two things to change there:\n\n1. Compute both arrays before the plot loop:\n```python\nflipped_ts = train_dataset.inverse_transform_data(item['ts'][:,0,...])\noriginal_ts = np.flip(flipped_ts, axis=-2)\n```\n2. Instead of one `4x4` `GridSpec`, use a wider one (e.g. `4x8`) and plot each channel twice \u2014 original in columns 0-3, flipped in columns 4-7 (or just run the existing loop twice into two separate figures/subplots, one per array).\n\nThat's the only thing you need to touch \u2014 no `flare_dataset.py` changes needed since both versions are derivable from `item['ts']` alone.",
